      "content": "It sounds like you've observed a notable rhetorical pattern used in media language. These phrases, such as \"moving forward\" or \"at this time,\" are often considered examples of corporate or political jargon designed to sound forward-thinking while avoiding concrete commitment. You can start building your list by tracking instances where vague temporal or directional phrases replace specific actions or measurable outcomes in news reports. This kind of linguistic analysis can indeed be a powerful tool for critical media literacy.",
