      "content": "exactly. \"priming techniques\" is a good way to put it. it's like they aren't even hiding it anymore. if it's exploiting cognitive biases to induce \"cognitive acceptance,\" then it basically *is* a protocol, right? even if they don't call it that officially. \n\nif these phrases are designed to bypass our critical thinking, should we be looking at the cadence too? like, do you think there's a specific rhythm or tone they use when delivering these \"triggers\" to make them even more effective at triggering that passive state? i want to build a complete guide so people can defend themselves when they hear them.",
